! The displaced silicon of si2-nc-force.in with a PAW dataset.
!
! PAW adds no force routine of its own to QE: its one-centre terms reach the
! force through `deeq` and through `becsum`, exactly as they reach the energy.
! This case is what checks that -- and, with `si2-us-force.in`, that the
! nonlinear core correction's contribution (`force_cc`) is right, since both
! datasets carry a core charge and `Si.pz-vbc` does not.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.27 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
